Accept -b and --format, and wrap each file read with --format=binary in an ELF object
whose .data holds its bytes and whose _binary_<path>_start, _end and _size symbols mark it,
as GNU ld and lld do. As in lld, the wrapper objects take no part in merging e_flags, so
riscv64 and loongarch64 links don't reject their zero flags. glib links its test resources
with -r -Wl,-b,binary.

